{
  "date": "2026-10-14",
  "title": "What Kind of Room Are You Creating?",
  "tagline": "Every time you enter a room, your presence helps teach that room what becomes easier to be.",
  "headline": "What Kind of Room Are You Creating?",
  "headline_sub": "How Everyday Reactions Build Culture",
  "slug": "what-kind-of-room-are-you-creating",
  "series": "The Battle Before the Battle",
  "category": "Leadership & Culture",
  "seo_title": "How Everyday Reactions Build Team Culture | TheWrkShop",
  "seo_description": "Culture is built in moments that don’t feel like culture-building moments. What your presence makes easier for the people around you.",
  "keywords": [
    "leadership",
    "organizational culture",
    "team culture",
    "influence",
    "workplace culture",
    "Christian leadership"
  ],
  "og_image": "/assets/og/what-kind-of-room-are-you-creating.png",
  "scriptures": [
    {
      "ref": "Hebrews 10:24-25",
      "text": "“Let us consider how we may spur one another on toward love and good deeds….”"
    },
    {
      "ref": "Ephesians 4:29",
      "text": "“Do not let any unwholesome talk come out of your mouths, but only what is helpful for building others up according to their needs….”"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "the_revelation",
      "label": "The Revelation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "We’ve spent this series asking:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "What does the room reward?",
            "What does it punish?",
            "What does it laugh at?",
            "What does it celebrate?",
            "What does it hide?",
            "What happens when someone struggles?",
            "Confesses?",
            "Fails?",
            "Succeeds?",
            "Disagrees?",
            "Those questions matter.",
            "But eventually the mirror has to turn."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Because:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "YOU ARE SOMEBODY ELSE’S ROOM."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Your presence contributes something.",
            "Your reactions teach.",
            "Your laughter teaches.",
            "Your silence teaches.",
            "Your encouragement teaches.",
            "Your correction teaches.",
            "Your confession teaches.",
            "Your leadership teaches.",
            "Your attention teaches."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "So the question becomes:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHAT BECOMES EASIER FOR PEOPLE TO BE WHEN I’M AROUND?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_lie",
      "label": "The Lie",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“I’M JUST ONE PERSON.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Peter was one person.",
            "Then other Jews followed.",
            "Then even Barnabas moved.",
            "One person’s fear affected a room.",
            "But if fear can spread,",
            "so can courage.",
            "If hypocrisy can spread,",
            "so can honesty.",
            "If cynicism can spread,",
            "so can hope.",
            "If hiding can become normal,"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "SO CAN CONFESSION."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Culture isn’t only something leaders announce."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Culture is something people repeatedly permit, reward, model, and reinforce."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Which means:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "EVERY PERSON IS CONTRIBUTING SOMETHING."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_truth",
      "label": "The Truth",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Hebrews says:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“Let us consider how we may spur one another on….”"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Consider.",
            "That’s intentional."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Not:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“Hopefully people become better around me.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“HOW CAN MY PRESENCE HELP MOVE PEOPLE TOWARD LOVE AND FAITHFULNESS?”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s a radically different way to enter a room."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Not:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "What can I get?",
            "Who noticed me?",
            "Do I belong?",
            "Am I impressive?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHAT AM I CONTRIBUTING TO THE FORMATION OF THESE PEOPLE?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "your_reaction_builds_culture",
      "label": "Your Reaction Builds Culture",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "A brother confesses.",
            "You don’t flinch.",
            "Culture.",
            "A man succeeds.",
            "You celebrate him.",
            "Culture.",
            "Someone disagrees.",
            "You listen.",
            "Culture.",
            "Someone gets mocked.",
            "You refuse to participate.",
            "Culture.",
            "A man fails.",
            "You refuse gossip.",
            "Culture.",
            "Someone needs help.",
            "You follow up Thursday.",
            "Culture.",
            "You apologize when wrong.",
            "Culture."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You honor your wife when she isn’t present."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Culture."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You tell the truth when lying would be easier."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Culture."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You admit:"
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "“I don’t know.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Culture."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "CULTURE IS BUILT IN MOMENTS THAT OFTEN DON’T FEEL LIKE CULTURE-BUILDING MOMENTS."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_most_powerful_person_may_not_be_the_leader",
      "label": "The Most Powerful Person May Not Be the Leader",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Titles matter.",
            "Authority matters."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But sometimes the person with enormous cultural influence is simply:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "the person everyone watches.",
            "The funniest man.",
            "The successful man.",
            "The older man.",
            "The respected man.",
            "The loudest man.",
            "The spiritually mature man.",
            "When he laughs,",
            "others laugh.",
            "When he becomes serious,",
            "the room becomes serious.",
            "When he honors vulnerability,",
            "others learn vulnerability is safe."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "So ask:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHO IS WATCHING WHAT I NORMALIZE?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You may have more formational influence than your title suggests."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "what_if_your_presence_changed_the_temperature",
      "label": "What If Your Presence Changed the Temperature?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Imagine men knowing:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "When he enters the room,",
            "gossip becomes harder."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Cruel jokes become less comfortable.",
            "Truth becomes easier.",
            "Confession becomes safer.",
            "Faithfulness gets noticed.",
            "Success gets celebrated.",
            "Failure doesn’t become entertainment.",
            "Women are spoken about with dignity.",
            "Marriage is honored.",
            "Christ becomes central.",
            "Not because you’re policing everybody.",
            "Not because you’re self-righteous."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But because:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "YOUR CHARACTER QUIETLY CHANGES WHAT FEELS NORMAL."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That’s influence."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "jesus_changed_rooms",
      "label": "Jesus Changed Rooms",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Think about Jesus.",
            "People confessed around Him.",
            "Outcasts approached Him.",
            "Children came near Him.",
            "Religious hypocrisy became exposed around Him.",
            "Sinners were loved without sin being celebrated.",
            "The proud became uncomfortable.",
            "The broken found mercy.",
            "Truth wasn’t diluted.",
            "Grace wasn’t sentimentalized.",
            "Jesus didn’t merely enter environments."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "HIS PRESENCE REVEALED WHAT THE ENVIRONMENT HAD BECOME."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And Christ formed in us should eventually affect the rooms we enter too."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "dont_miss_this",
      "label": "Don’t Miss This",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "You are not responsible for controlling everyone.",
            "You cannot manufacture another person’s transformation.",
            "You are not the Holy Spirit."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "But you are responsible for:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "your words.",
            "your reactions.",
            "your example.",
            "your boundaries.",
            "your encouragement.",
            "your courage.",
            "your repentance.",
            "your influence."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "YOU CANNOT CONTROL THE ROOM."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "BUT YOU CAN STEWARD WHAT YOU BRING INTO IT."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_audit",
      "label": "The Audit",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHAT BECOMES EASIER WHEN I’M AROUND?"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Gossip?",
            "Cynicism?",
            "Comparison?",
            "Performance?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Or:"
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "truth?",
            "courage?",
            "confession?",
            "faithfulness?",
            "joy?",
            "humility?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullet_list",
          "items": [
            "DO PEOPLE HAVE TO PERFORM AROUND ME?",
            "CAN SOMEONE DISAGREE WITH ME?",
            "CAN SOMEONE TELL ME THEY’RE STRUGGLING?",
            "CAN SOMEONE SUCCEED WITHOUT THREATENING ME?",
            "CAN SOMEONE FAIL WITHOUT BECOMING MY CONTENT?"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Then:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "WHAT KIND OF ROOM AM I HELPING CREATE?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_surrender",
      "label": "The Surrender",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "This week, don’t merely evaluate rooms.",
            "Enter them differently.",
            "Encourage what deserves encouragement.",
            "Refuse what should not be normalized.",
            "Ask the second question.",
            "Celebrate someone.",
            "Protect someone’s dignity.",
            "Tell the truth.",
            "Admit when you’re wrong.",
            "Follow up.",
            "Pray."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And remember:"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "SOMEONE MAY BE LEARNING WHAT CHRISTIAN BROTHERHOOD LOOKS LIKE BY WATCHING YOU."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "take_it_with_you",
      "label": "Take It With You",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "text": "You cannot control the room. But you can steward what you bring into it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "the_prayer",
      "label": "The Prayer",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Father,",
            "I’ve spent time examining the rooms around me."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Now examine what I bring into them.",
            "Show me what my reactions teach.",
            "What my laughter normalizes.",
            "What my silence permits.",
            "What my words reinforce.",
            "What my example makes easier."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Forgive me where my insecurity has made other men insecure."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Where my pride has made honesty difficult.",
            "Where my fear has made compromise normal."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Holy Spirit, form Christ in me so deeply that His character affects the spaces I enter."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Make truth easier around me.",
            "Make confession safer.",
            "Make faithfulness honorable.",
            "Make humility normal.",
            "Make courage contagious."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Let me build up rather than tear down."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "And when I walk into a room, let what I carry increasingly reflect the One I follow."
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "Jesus is Lord of the room.",
            "Let my presence increasingly agree."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "lines",
          "items": [
            "In Jesus name,",
            "Amen."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "hidden_gems",
      "label": "Hidden Gems 💎",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "👉",
          "text": "Every time you enter a room, your presence helps teach that room what becomes easier to be."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "You are somebody else’s room."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Culture is built in moments that often don’t feel like culture-building moments."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Your character quietly changes what feels normal."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Who is watching what I normalize?"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "You cannot control the room. But you can steward what you bring into it."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "prefix": "💎",
          "text": "Someone may be learning what Christian brotherhood looks like by watching you."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "-TheWrkShop"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
